#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG Catalog and governance plane"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "One catalog of record for tables, files and functions, enforcing grants, tags and policies."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: data · depends on: [CAP-TABLES]{1}, [CAP-IDENTITY]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "The catalog is the one place that knows about every dataset, and it decides who may read which rows and columns."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "A policy that one engine enforces and another ignores isn't really a policy. Granting access only to groups keeps it reviewable ([P5]{1}), and having one catalog per domain keeps ownership clear and each dataset in one place ([P6]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Namespaces, with `<domain>_<env>` catalogs and `<product>_<layer>` schemas inside each domain."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Grants, governed tags, row filters and column masks."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Credentials vended to engines."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Engines differ in what they enforce. Route protected tables only through the engines that enforce the policies, and deny access to the rest."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "One catalog of record lists every table, volume of files and function, whichever engine created it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "An inventory of storage locations has no table unknown to the catalog."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Catalogs are named domain by environment (`<domain>_<env>`); a product is a set of schemas inside its domain, and data shared across domains is promoted to its owning domain and read from there, never copied."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Catalog and schema names match the pattern; no table is a copy of another domain's."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Grants go only to groups, and production objects are owned by groups."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "A query of grants and owners finds no individual user."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Governed tags (provenance, classification) can be set only by principals granted the right to assign them."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Negative test: an analyst cannot set a classification tag."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Row filters and column masks are enforced on every read path that serves protected data; an engine that cannot enforce them is denied those tables."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Read a protected table through each engine as a scoped user; each returns only the scoped rows or is refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Engines receive short-lived, scoped storage credentials from the catalog, never long-lived storage keys."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Engine configuration holds no storage key; credentials observed in use expire."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "CAP-CATALOG.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Every authenticated user may browse metadata, so data can be found without being readable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "A user with no data grants can list catalog objects but not read them."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-catalog.md
msgid "Standards"
msgstr ""

